Welcome to DreamStudio Manual Support!

DSMAN (.dsman) is a notebook collection of manual files that comes shipped with
DreamStudio's standard installation. You can access files and read documentations
easily using DreamStudio Terminal for Documentations. 

Getting Started:
To search any topic, you have several options: 
1. Type-in the name of the topic you would like to search for.
2. Type-in the name of the command you are looking for, any type of DreamStudio's 
   commands would work whether inside this terminal or in other DreamStudio's 
   terminals.
3. You can also extend your search by looking inside manual files, not just only
   by file's name, that is by typing the command: 

   >>> Search-Topic {topic-word}
   {topic-word}: The word you are searching for.

All Commands: 
This is a fast documentation of what each command is designed for:
1. help: shows help (already open now)
2. clear: clears the screen
3. exit: exits the tool

4. get-started: shows a welcome message with some topics mostly requested to start
   reading about right-away.
5. get-commands: shows all available commands (without documentation)

6. search-topic: searches files names, and occurrences of the word inside files to 
   find relavent match of the requested topic name.
7. search-several: searches files contents for a whole line. Be careful here: it 
   takes a full line so its occurrence might be less.

8. open-pdf: opens the PDF documentation manual in a dedicated PDF browser from the
   operating system.

You can also type in immediately the topic's name in the terminal if you are 
confident you can find it.

Further Documentation:
If you like PDF-Style documentations, you could read the PDF documentation manual
associated with the version you installed. 

